  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "3.1.0: Chrome also starts when the test runs as administrator (e.g. Visual Studio run as admin); before, Chrome relaunched itself without admin rights and the driver failed with \"Chrome instance exited\". New: BrowserOptions.ConfigureChrome and ConfigureFirefox, and the ChromeArguments / FirefoxArguments settings (VAF_ChromeArguments), add browser options while Testing.On<Chrome>() stays as it is. 3.0.0: .NET 10 alongside .NET Framework 4.7.2, with the same API. No test framework dependency: failed checks throw VafAssertionException, which NUnit 3 and 4, MSTest and xUnit report as a failed test. Only Selenium as a dependency. Settings from VAF_* environment variables or app.config. New: Testing.On(browser) for a browser created with settings (remote grid, extra arguments); LetsSaveScreenshotTo; AndAlso() also after a check; HTML report named per test; a .NET 5-9 project stops at build with error VAF0001. Removed: BrowserStack, the mobile types, WinFormApplication, InternetExplorer and the MSTest v1 screenshot overload. Upgrading from 2.x: see \"Migrating from 2.x\" in the README.",
